_dev\docs\_archive\security-audit.md-48-- **Impact**: Server can be coerced to make requests to internal network/services.
_dev\docs\_archive\security-audit.md-49-- **Recommended fix**: Enforce URL allowlist (or disable override in production), validate scheme/host/IP ranges, block localhost/private ranges if not needed.
_dev\docs\_archive\security-audit.md-50-
_dev\docs\_archive\security-audit.md-51-7. **High: Concurrency races on shared in-memory job dictionaries**
_dev\docs\_archive\security-audit.md:52:- **Problem**: Shared dicts are read/written from multiple threads without consistent locking.
_dev\docs\_archive\security-audit.md-53-- **Affected**: `studio/assets/routes.py:54`, `studio/assets/routes.py:174`, `studio/assets/routes.py:183`, `studio/editor/routes.py:30`, `studio/editor/routes.py:709`, `studio/editor/routes.py:812`
_dev\docs\_archive\security-audit.md-54-- **Severity**: High
_dev\docs\_archive\security-audit.md-55-- **Impact**: Inconsistent job states, lost updates, intermittent failures under concurrent use.
_dev\docs\_archive\security-audit.md-56-- **Recommended fix**: Use locks for all read/write accesses or move to thread-safe queue/store abstraction.
--
