_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md:138:### 4. Deterministic DAG execution (ready queue, not raw stack)
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md-139-
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md:140:Use a dependency-aware ready queue based on a validated DAG:
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md-141-
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md-142-1. Validate the workflow and requested execution scope.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md-143-2. Build adjacency and reverse-dependency maps once (Automa's O(1) `sourceHandle → targets` lookup).
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md-144-3. Determine the required subgraph for the requested run mode.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md:145:4. Add a node to the ready queue only when its required inputs are resolved or safely restored from cache — multi-input nodes (Assemble, Merge) wait for all connected inputs.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md-146-5. Use a stable tie-breaker (saved node order, then node ID) so plans and tests are deterministic.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md-147-6. Execute through adapters, persist results in `run_data[node_id]`, emit events, release downstream nodes.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md-148-7. V1 runs ready nodes sequentially; design the scheduler so bounded parallel execution of independent nodes can be added later without changing contracts.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md-149-
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md:150:Do not use a raw depth-first stack that can mishandle multi-input joins.
