I’ve settled the execution semantics around the frozen contract: every incoming data/control edge is a dependency, port values are resolved only after all predecessors finish, and the ready queue uses persisted node order with ID as a deterministic fallback. A disabled or otherwise skipped predecessor propagates a skip to its dependents, while independent branches continue. The project guard will be non-blocking and process-aware, with a staging API for atomic file publication.
